Subject: [PATCH] climbing: ingest gym logbook sessions and show them on a
 Climbing screen

POST /api/v1/ingest/climbing takes sessions from a climbing logbook app,
pushed by a client in a format FreeReps defines (server/specs/
climbing-ingest.md), into climbing_sessions and climbing_ascents
(migration 000040). Each push replaces the sessions it names, ascents
included, in one transaction. Grades are stored as the gym labels them,
with an optional client-supplied rank within that gym's scale.

Read back through GET /api/v1/climbing/sessions, the get_climbing_sessions
MCP tool, and a Climbing screen (desktop nav; linked from Workouts on the
phone). Reasoning in DECISIONS.md, 2026-10-20; pairing with Apple Health
climbing workouts is a ROADMAP row.

Verified: go build/vet/test, the storage integration suite against
TimescaleDB on PG (migrations 1-40 from empty), tools/lint.sh (0 issues),
frontend tsc + build, tools/check-docs.sh, and an end-to-end push of 23
real Arkose+ sessions (107 ascents) rendered on the new screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
